# Log group: aws/spans (CloudWatch Transaction Search). Traces: step 07 6ae5cbc4..., step 08 6ae5cc3b..., step 10 6ae5cca5..., step 11 6ae5cd1c...
# Stage 1 groups by spanId: Transaction Search can hold two records of one span (OTel span and X-Ray segment copy), and dedup cannot precede stats.
# How much does each tracing option record? Distinct spans, distinct span names and trace length per trace.
filter traceId in ["6ae5cbc4712cf6fd1703fd806783e1ad", "6ae5cc3b44cc9da909fe2c2e7aebf8f3", "6ae5cca544a55195411c3a0251cd3b9a", "6ae5cd1c75705e4c04ad9fe673a2a55e"]
| stats latest(name) as spanName, min(startTimeUnixNano) as s, max(endTimeUnixNano) as e by traceId, spanId
| stats count() as spans, count_distinct(spanName) as distinctNames, min(s) as firstStartNs, max(e) as lastEndNs by traceId
